From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:47:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mac80211: do not apply a suggested TTLM from an
 association response

ieee80211_assoc_success() takes every TTLM element of an Association
Response as the established advertised TTLM. mac80211 adds no TTLM
element to the request, but user space can. IEEE 802.11be-2024
35.3.7.2.3 then gives the element of the response another meaning:
where the AP MLD advertises no established TTLM and rejects the
requested mapping, the element suggests a preferred mapping, and "the
default TTLM shall be used during the association". The station instead
applies the suggestion, and fails the association where the suggestion
maps the TIDs to different links or holds one direction only, although
"An ML (re)setup can be successful even if the TTLM negotiation
embedded in the ML (re)setup procedure is not successful".

Where the request carried a TTLM element and the Beacon or Probe
Response frame of the association link holds no established TTLM, keep
the default mapping. Where the AP MLD advertises an established TTLM,
the response carries that mapping, so keep applying it then.

The scan result can be older than the mapping. Apply an established
mapping from a Beacon frame where the station still uses the default
mapping, so that a wrong decision at the association does not last.

Fixes: aebc29dec67a ("wifi: mac80211: apply advertised TTLM from association response")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>

--- a/net/mac80211/mlme.c
+++ b/net/mac80211/mlme.c
@@ -6981,18 +6981,43 @@ ieee80211_parse_adv_t2l(struct ieee80211
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static bool ieee80211_adv_ttlm_established(struct cfg80211_bss *cbss)
+{
+	const struct cfg80211_bss_ies *ies;
+	const struct element *elem;
+	bool ret = false;
+
+	rcu_read_lock();
+	ies = rcu_dereference(cbss->ies);
+	for_each_element_extid(elem, WLAN_EID_EXT_TID_TO_LINK_MAPPING,
+			       ies->data, ies->len) {
+		if (elem->datalen >= 2 &&
+		    !(elem->data[1] & IEEE80211_TTLM_CONTROL_SWITCH_TIME_PRESENT)) {
+			ret = true;
+			break;
+		}
+	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
+
+	return ret;
+}
+
 /*
- * We do not support setting a negotiated TTLM during association. As such,
- * we can assume that if there is a TTLM, then it is the currently active
- * advertised TTLM. In that case, there must be exactly one TTLM that does
- * not have a switch time set. This mapping should also leave us with at
- * least one usable link.
+ * We do not support setting a negotiated TTLM during association, but user
+ * space may add a TTLM element to the request. Where the AP MLD advertises
+ * no established TTLM, a TTLM in the response then only suggests a mapping,
+ * and the default mapping applies (IEEE 802.11be-2024 35.3.7.2.3).
+ * Otherwise a TTLM is the currently active advertised TTLM. In that case,
+ * there must be exactly one TTLM that does not have a switch time set. This
+ * mapping should also leave us with at least one usable link.
  */
 static bool ieee80211_assoc_adv_ttlm(struct ieee80211_sub_if_data *sdata,
 				     struct ieee802_11_elems *elems,
 				     u16 valid_links, u16 *dormant_links)
 {
 	struct ieee80211_mgd_assoc_data *assoc_data = sdata->u.mgd.assoc_data;
+	struct cfg80211_bss *assoc_bss =
+		assoc_data->link[assoc_data->assoc_link_id].bss;
 	struct ieee80211_adv_ttlm_info *ttlm_info = &sdata->u.mgd.ttlm_info;
 
 	memset(ttlm_info, 0, sizeof(*ttlm_info));
@@ -7000,6 +7025,15 @@ static bool ieee80211_assoc_adv_ttlm(str
 	if (!elems->ttlm_num)
 		return true;
 
+	if (cfg80211_find_ext_elem(WLAN_EID_EXT_TID_TO_LINK_MAPPING,
+				   sdata->u.mgd.assoc_req_ies,
+				   sdata->u.mgd.assoc_req_ies_len) &&
+	    !ieee80211_adv_ttlm_established(assoc_bss)) {
+		sdata_info(sdata,
+			   "TTLM in association response suggests a mapping, using the default mapping\n");
+		return true;
+	}
+
 	if (elems->ttlm_num > 1) {
 		sdata_info(sdata,
 			   "More than one advertised TTLM in association response\n");
@@ -7937,6 +7971,23 @@ static void ieee80211_process_adv_ttlm(s
 			return;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * The association decides by a scan result that can be older
+		 * than the established mapping, so apply it from here.
+		 */
+		if (!ttlm_info.switch_time &&
+		    !sdata->u.mgd.ttlm_info.active &&
+		    !sdata->u.mgd.ttlm_info.switch_time &&
+		    !sdata->vif.neg_ttlm.valid &&
+		    (ttlm_info.map & sdata->vif.valid_links)) {
+			sdata->u.mgd.ttlm_info = ttlm_info;
+			sdata->u.mgd.ttlm_info.switch_time = 1;
+			wiphy_hrtimer_work_queue(sdata->local->hw.wiphy,
+						 &sdata->u.mgd.ttlm_work,
+						 us_to_ktime(0));
+			return;
+		}
+
 		if (ttlm_info.switch_time) {
 			u16 beacon_ts_tu, st_tu, delay;
 			u64 delay_usec;
